## 1. Executive Summary

DevDock is a self-hosted, full-stack developer platform that combines source-code repository management, real-time collaboration, AI-assisted development, and social networking into a single cohesive product. It is designed to give teams and individual developers a private, extensible alternative to GitHub/GitLab with built-in AI tooling, live code editing, messaging, and a gamified contribution system.

### Core Value Propositions
- **Own your data** — runs on-premise with a MySQL backend and local file storage
- **AI-first workflow** — integrated Groq/LLaMA AI assistant for code suggestions, explanations, and automated QA
- **Real-time everything** — Socket.io powers live messaging, presence, and collaborative editing
- **Social developer network** — follow, message, collaborate, and track contributions like a professional social platform
- **GitHub bridge** — import, push, pull, and sync repositories directly with GitHub

