## 3. Target Audience & User Personas

### Persona 1 — Solo Developer
- Wants a private GitHub alternative to host personal projects
- Uses AI assistant for quick code help without leaving the platform
- Tracks contribution streaks to stay motivated

### Persona 2 — Small Engineering Team
- Needs role-based file collaboration (viewer / editor / owner)
- Creates pull requests and issues to coordinate work
- Relies on real-time messaging and live editor for pair programming

### Persona 3 — Open-Source Contributor
- Explores public repositories and stars notable projects
- Follows other developers and tracks their activity
- Forks repositories and syncs changes back via GitHub integration

### Persona 4 — QA Engineer / Team Lead
- Runs automated static analysis on repository files
- Generates AI test plans and QA reports with defect severity levels
- Reviews quality scores and tracks defect history over time

