## 6. Feature Specifications

### 6.1 Authentication & Identity

#### 6.1.1 Email/Password Registration & Login
- User registers with `username`, `email`, and `password`
- Password hashed with bcryptjs (salt rounds: 10)
- On login, server issues a signed JWT; client stores it in localStorage
- `POST /api/auth/register` — validate uniqueness of username and email
- `POST /api/auth/login` — returns `{ token, user }`

#### 6.1.2 Google OAuth 2.0
- Flow: `/auth/google` → Google consent → `/auth/google/callback`
- Account linking: if email already exists, Google ID is attached to the existing account
- New accounts are created automatically with a unique username derived from the Google display name
- On success, redirect to `/auth-success?token=<jwt>`

#### 6.1.3 GitHub OAuth 2.0
- Flow: `/auth/github` → GitHub consent → `/auth/github/callback`
- GitHub access token is AES-encrypted and stored in `users.github_access_token`
- `github_login` and `github_connected` fields updated on every login
- Token refreshed on each OAuth callback to stay current

#### 6.1.4 Password Recovery
- `ForgotPassword` and `ResetPassword` UI components available
- `SetPassword` component handles first-time password set for OAuth-only accounts

#### 6.1.5 JWT Middleware
- `middleware/auth.js` — `authenticateToken()` verifies and injects `req.user`
- Optional auth pattern used on public routes to optionally enrich responses for logged-in users

