### 6.2 Repository Management

#### Core CRUD
| Operation | Endpoint | Auth |
|-----------|----------|------|
| Create repo | `POST /api/repos` | Required |
| List own repos | `GET /api/repos` | Required |
| List public repos | `GET /api/repos/public` | Optional |
| Get repo by ID | `GET /api/repos/:id` | Optional (private = Required) |
| Update repo | `PUT /api/repos/:id` | Required (owner) |
| Delete repo | `DELETE /api/repos/:id` | Required (owner) |

#### Visibility
- `public` — discoverable, readable by all
- `private` — visible only to owner and collaborators

#### Stars
- `POST /api/repos/:id/star` — star a repo (unique constraint prevents duplicates)
- `DELETE /api/repos/:id/star` — unstar
- `GET /api/repos/:id/starred` — check star status
- `GET /api/repos/starred` — get all repos starred by current user
- Star events trigger `BadgeService.checkAllBadges()` to potentially award `first_star` badge

#### Pinned Repositories
- Users can pin up to N repositories to their public profile
- `GET /api/users/:username/pinned` — get pinned repos
- `POST /api/pinned` / `DELETE /api/pinned/:repoId` — manage pins
- Pinning a repo awards the `first_pinned` badge

#### Repository Actions Log
- Every CRUD action (create, update, delete, star, upload) is recorded in `repository_actions` table
- Powers the Insights tab and activity feed
- `GET /api/repos/:id/actions` returns paginated log

