### 6.5 Messaging System

#### Architecture
- REST API for CRUD + Socket.io for real-time delivery
- All message routes require JWT auth (`router.use(authenticateToken)`)
- Rate limiting: max 5 socket messages per user per second (in-memory)

#### Conversations
| Endpoint | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `GET /api/messages/conversations` | Sidebar list: one row per partner, last message, unread count |
| `GET /api/messages/messages/:partnerId` | Full message thread, paginated |
| `POST /api/messages/send` | Send a text message |
| `POST /api/messages/send-image` | Send an image (multipart, max 10 MB) |
| `POST /api/messages/mark-read/:partnerId` | Mark all messages from partner as read |
| `GET /api/messages/unread-count` | Total unread count for Navbar badge |
| `GET /api/messages/search-users?q=` | Search users to start a new conversation |

#### Real-time Events (Socket.io)
| Event | Direction | Payload |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `send_private_message` | client → server | `{ receiverId, content, type }` |
| `private_message` | server → client | full message object |
| `message_seen` | client → server | `{ partnerId }` |
| `messages_seen` | server → client | `{ by: userId }` |
| `user_online` | server → all | `{ userId }` |
| `user_offline` | server → all | `{ userId }` |

#### Messenger UI
- `messenger/` component directory contains dedicated messenger pages
- Sidebar with conversation list and online indicators
- Message bubbles with image preview, timestamps, and read receipts
- Typing indicator support

