### 6.8 GitHub Integration

#### Connection Flow
1. User connects GitHub via `/auth/github` OAuth
2. Access token encrypted (AES) and stored in `users.github_access_token`
3. `GitHubConnect` component shows connection status; `GitHubConnectSuccess` handles callback

#### Sync Operations
| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/api/github/status` | GET | Check if token is valid |
| `/api/github/list-repos` | GET | List user's GitHub repositories |
| `/api/github/import` | POST | Import a GitHub repo as a new DevDock repo |
| `/api/github/sync-push/:repoId` | POST | Push DevDock repo to GitHub (creates if not exists) |
| `/api/github/sync-pull/:repoId` | POST | Pull latest from GitHub into DevDock repo |
| `/api/github/link/:repoId` | POST | Link DevDock repo to an existing GitHub repo |
| `/api/github/link/:repoId` | DELETE | Unlink |
| `/api/github/link/:repoId` | GET | Get link info |
| `/api/github/sync-history/:repoId` | GET | Last 20 sync log entries |

#### Error Handling
- 401 → Token invalid/expired, prompt reconnect
- 429 → Rate limit hit, show retry countdown
- 403 → Forbidden (scope issue)
- 404 → Repo not found or private

`GitHubSyncPanel` and `GitHubExplorer` components expose all sync operations from within a repository.

