### 6.11 Live Collaborative Editor

#### Architecture
- `LiveEditor` feature spins up a separate Vite-based frontend (`live-text-editor-main`) on port **5173**
- Backend for live editor runs on port **5003**
- `liveEditor.js` route manages process lifecycle:
  - Detects if already running (port check)
  - Spawns `npm run dev` in the live editor directory
  - Returns a redirect URL once the port is ready (max 10s wait with 500ms polling)

#### Endpoints
| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `POST /api/live-editor/start` | POST | Start live editor process |
| `GET /api/live-editor/status` | GET | Check if live editor is running |
| `POST /api/live-editor/stop` | POST | Stop live editor process |

#### User Experience
- `AutomatedLiveEditorButton` component triggers start and redirects the user
- `CodeEditorCollab` handles in-platform real-time editing sessions
- Users share edit sessions via Socket.io rooms scoped to file ID

