## 9. Non-Functional Requirements

### Performance
- API response time < 300ms for all read operations under normal load
- File upload limit: 10 MB per file for code files; 10 MB for chat images
- Socket.io rate limit: 5 messages/second/user to prevent spam flooding
- AI endpoint rate limit: 5 requests/minute/user
- Database indexes on all FK columns and frequently queried fields (user_id, repo_id, is_read, created_at)
- `CacheService` used to avoid redundant analysis runs on unchanged code

### Scalability
- Stateless JWT authentication supports horizontal scaling of the API server
- Socket.io server may require sticky sessions or a Redis adapter for multi-instance deployment
- File storage is local (`uploads/`); migrate to S3-compatible storage for production scale

### Availability
- `kill_ports.bat` / `npm run kill-ports` scripts for clean restarts during development
- `npm run dev-safe` kills lingering processes before starting
- `cloudflared/` directory indicates support for Cloudflare Tunnel for public exposure without open firewall ports

### Maintainability
- Modular route files (one file per feature domain)
- Dedicated service layer (`/services/`) for business logic
- Separate model layer (`/models/`) for database operations
- Migration scripts (`/migrations/`) for schema evolution without data loss

