## 10. Security Requirements

### Authentication & Authorization
- Passwords never stored in plaintext — bcryptjs with 10 salt rounds
- JWT signed with `process.env.JWT_SECRET` — must be ≥ 32 characters in production
- GitHub OAuth tokens AES-encrypted at rest (`utils/tokenCrypto`); never returned to client
- All mutation endpoints require `authenticateToken` middleware
- Ownership checks enforced before update/delete on repos, files, PRs, issues

### Input Validation & Sanitization
- Social link URLs sanitized via `sanitizeUrl()` — blocks `javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:` URI schemes
- File upload restricted by MIME type and size in Multer config
- SQL queries use parameterized statements (mysql2 prepared queries) — no string interpolation
- User search input sanitized with `LIKE` + `%` escape via parameterized queries

### Access Control
- Public repos readable by anyone; private repos check ownership or collaborator membership
- Collaboration role check on all file-scoped operations
- Admin routes protected by `requireAdmin` middleware (username allowlist from env)
- Blocked users cannot message or access certain profile data

### Rate Limiting
- In-memory rate limiter on Socket.io messages (5 msg/sec/user)
- In-memory rate limiter on AI/Testing endpoints (5 req/min/user)
- Consider adding `express-rate-limit` for HTTP endpoints in production

### Network
- CORS configured (review `origin: '*'` in Socket.io — restrict to known origins in production)
- HTTPS enforced when deployed behind Cloudflare Tunnel
- Environment variables never committed (`.env` in `.gitignore`)

